WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.914
A synthetic fact is an interpretation derived from evidence. Read these two notes. One

00:00:05.914 --> 00:00:11.622
says customs has cleared, but nobody will arrange collection. The other describes a

00:00:11.622 --> 00:00:17.329
required lab result with a named person following up. Both records are delayed. The

00:00:17.329 --> 00:00:21.800
ownership problem is something an AI has to infer from the notes.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:31.511
Here is the resulting fact as JSON. Entity identifies the shipment, attribute names

00:00:31.511 --> 00:00:37.424
the question, and the typed value holds the classification. The explanation and

00:00:37.424 --> 00:00:43.561
citations let us inspect its basis. This recording uses a prepared AI example. The

00:00:43.561 --> 00:00:48.725
classification is a hypothesis; it does not grant access to anything.

00:00:52.225 --> 00:00:57.852
A bridge connects the shipment identifier to the fact’s shipment identifier. That

00:00:57.852 --> 00:01:03.689
makes the synthetic facts available as a related list inside the lens. These are two

00:01:03.689 --> 00:01:09.178
field maps connected by a serializable definition. A narrower lens can hide the

00:01:09.178 --> 00:01:13.625
relation or restrict its fields, just as it can for source data.

00:01:17.125 --> 00:01:23.086
Now combine them. The all group requires Express priority, at least two customs holds,

00:01:23.086 --> 00:01:28.769
and an ownership-handoff fact. Inside the fact condition, attribute and value must

00:01:28.769 --> 00:01:34.176
match on the same row. We are applying the rules engine to the interpretation,

00:01:34.176 --> 00:01:36.325
alongside the original records.

00:01:39.825 --> 00:01:45.451
First, To Prisma retrieves the source records permitted by the lens. The engine joins

00:01:45.451 --> 00:01:50.813
the permitted synthetic facts to those records, then Check evaluates the combined

00:01:50.813 --> 00:01:56.506
predicate. Two shipments match. A ranked-window question about the second-longest hold

00:01:56.506 --> 00:02:00.875
leaves one. You can inspect the rule and the result at each stage.

00:02:04.375 --> 00:02:10.060
Now the platform removes the synthetic-fact relation from its lens. Our combined rule

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:15.812
still references that relation. It was valid before; under the inherited narrowing, it

00:02:15.812 --> 00:02:21.563
is invalid. That is rule staleness. The source records are still there, and an allowed

00:02:21.563 --> 00:02:26.981
source-only rule still works. We have to revise the combined predicate to fit the

00:02:26.981 --> 00:02:30.125
lens. Waiting or refreshing does not repair it.

00:02:33.625 --> 00:02:39.307
An invented fact for another customer’s shipment cannot bring that shipment into the

00:02:39.307 --> 00:02:45.057
result. The engine checks the entity, source evidence, and lens instance before using

00:02:45.057 --> 00:02:50.807
a fact. The agent can propose an interpretation and a predicate. It cannot use either

00:02:50.807 --> 00:02:53.175
one to widen the underlying access.
